// Package cassette records HTTP calls as [Interactions], stored as JSON, and replays them.
//
// To mock a client in tests, or to record its calls, use [Replay]: it is the [http.RoundTripper] for both, and
// there is no need to write one of your own.
//
//   - Mock: [Replay](ias) answers each request from the recording it matches, and fails any other without
//     touching the network. A client generated by openapi-codegen takes it through its WithHTTPClient option.
//   - Record: [Replay](ias, [RecordMisses](nil)) sends what has no recording, and [Recorder.Interactions] holds
//     the calls to write with [Interactions.WriteFile].
//   - Test strictly: [InOrder] and [CompareHeaders] check every call against its recording in turn, and
//     [Recorder.Unused] tells what was never called.
//
// Writing to a file always masks credentials first, see [Interactions.Mask].
package cassette
